b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316961" :question/id #uuid "8801db2a-1b08-5cda-b295-4573e6575f4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-316961" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316961/field-1" "q-316961/field-2" "q-316961/field-3" "q-316961/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316983/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "e95b0c43-bafa-5ff5-a880-447b32e634c4" :answer/type :answer.type/m